<title>USA: NY business loans fell $103 mln in Nov 6 week.</title>
<headline>NY business loans fell $103 mln in Nov 6 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $103 million to $42.726 billion in the week ended November 6, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $92 million to $42.987 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $2.715 billion to $756.190 billion.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
